1
00:00:39,460 --> 00:00:41,940
A strange feeling

2
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:47,720
So, walking along the arcade guide tiles

3
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:53,460
I tried walking only on the black parts

4
00:00:55,960 --> 00:00:59,640
Everyone was a child once,

5
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:01,720
but everyone forgets

6
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:05,780
the politicians with
their self-important faces

7
00:01:05,780 --> 00:01:09,100
and the aunties with blue
eyeshadow above their eyes

8
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:12,080
Try turning the corner, come on

9
00:01:13,060 --> 00:01:14,660
that corner over there

10
00:01:15,880 --> 00:01:19,880
You can meet everyone, everyone

11
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:24,640
Over there is Kameari

12
00:01:25,740 --> 00:01:27,960
It's surely Kameari

13
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:32,980
Come on, everyone, to our town

14
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:34,640
Thank you

15
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:39,780
Ryotsu Taxi, now in service

16
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:46,160
Nakagawa, you've been a big help.

17
00:01:46,160 --> 00:01:49,600
I never expected to run into
you in front of headquarters.

18
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:51,680
It really is a coincidence, Chief.

19
00:01:52,140 --> 00:01:54,240
Did you have a meeting at headquarters?

20
00:01:55,320 --> 00:02:00,000
It's the general meeting about the taxi robberies that
have been happening all over the city lately, right?

21
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:03,940
We've been getting a lot of
cases within our jurisdiction too.

22
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:09,440
Nakagawa, no cell phones while driving!

23
00:02:09,440 --> 00:02:11,200
Of course, I know that.

24
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:15,260
Chief, my car phone is hands-free.

25
00:02:15,260 --> 00:02:16,460
Hands-free.

26
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:19,680
Yes, this is Nakagawa.

27
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:20,560
It's me.

28
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:23,160
What is it, senpai?

29
00:02:23,160 --> 00:02:24,680
Hold on a moment.

30
00:02:24,680 --> 00:02:27,000
Your voice just came out of the speaker!

31
00:02:27,580 --> 00:02:29,720
I'm using the car stereo speakers.

32
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:33,320
The microphone is right here,
on the steering wheel.

33
00:02:34,620 --> 00:02:37,740
Sorry, sorry.
I just ran into a friend, you see.

34
00:02:37,740 --> 00:02:39,000
Are you on patrol?

35
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,640
Patrol? Don't be ridiculous.

36
00:02:41,640 --> 00:02:45,880
On a gorgeous day like this, perfect for gambling,
who'd want to be stuck on patrol?

37
00:02:45,880 --> 00:02:46,620
What?

38
00:02:47,660 --> 00:02:50,780
What was that weird voice just now?
Is someone with you?

39
00:02:50,780 --> 00:02:59,460
N-no, I'm driving right now and was listening to the radio,
so I'll turn the volume down.

40
00:03:00,020 --> 00:03:01,320
It's just the radio.

41
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:05,140
I think he's in a car right now.

42
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:05,980
Well...

43
00:03:06,860 --> 00:03:08,480
This sound is the hint.

44
00:03:11,460 --> 00:03:13,720
I can hear waves and an engine, can't I?

45
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:16,460
Are you riding a motorboat or something?

46
00:03:16,460 --> 00:03:18,760
You're getting warm, Nakagawa.

47
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:20,140
Hint number two.

48
00:03:20,140 --> 00:03:23,700
It's a place where men who dream
of getting rich quick gather.

49
00:03:23,700 --> 00:03:26,080
Don't tell me it's a racetrack or something.

50
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:26,860
No, nothing.

51
00:03:27,440 --> 00:03:30,120
Idiot, would a racetrack
have the sound of waves?

52
00:03:30,120 --> 00:03:31,300
It's a boatrace venue.

53
00:03:31,300 --> 00:03:31,880
What?

54
00:03:34,820 --> 00:03:38,120
I was planning to win back my losses from the horse races on Sunday,
you see.

55
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:43,760
Senpai,
you really shouldn't talk for so long.

56
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:46,560
Go, go, go! Third place!

57
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:49,120
Idiot, idiot! What are you doing?

58
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:50,760
No good, no good, no good!

59
00:03:50,760 --> 00:03:53,140
You idiot, give me my money back!

60
00:03:53,140 --> 00:03:55,720
What are you going to do about this?

61
00:03:57,040 --> 00:03:59,460
Senpai, your voice is too loud.

62
00:03:59,460 --> 00:04:01,920
I'm listening through the car stereo,
you know.

63
00:04:03,320 --> 00:04:04,100
Sorry, sorry.

64
00:04:04,100 --> 00:04:05,920
Still, that makes me so angry.

65
00:04:05,920 --> 00:04:07,480
You bastard!

66
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:09,080
Damn it!

67
00:04:09,080 --> 00:04:11,800
Senpai?

68
00:04:12,100 --> 00:04:12,980
What's wrong?

69
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:14,400
It's nothing. Just a little something.

70
00:04:17,280 --> 00:04:17,940
Nakagawa

71
00:04:17,940 --> 00:04:19,800
Do you know where you are right now?

72
00:04:20,120 --> 00:04:21,420
Isn't it the boatrace venue?

73
00:04:21,780 --> 00:04:24,980
I'm asking where inside
the boatrace venue you are.

74
00:04:24,980 --> 00:04:27,460
Seems like I went into some room.

75
00:04:28,100 --> 00:04:28,860
Whoa.

76
00:04:30,360 --> 00:04:31,520
Idiot!

77
00:04:33,320 --> 00:04:34,220
Who would do something like that?

78
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:36,360
What's with you all of a sudden?

79
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:38,800
Even the part that was about to come
out got cut off by the time limit!

80
00:04:40,020 --> 00:04:41,980
But that voice just now sounds familiar.

81
00:04:41,980 --> 00:04:43,060
It's me.

82
00:04:43,060 --> 00:04:44,340
It's Ohara.

83
00:04:44,340 --> 00:04:45,200
Chief.

84
00:04:45,780 --> 00:04:47,840
Why are you here, Chief?

85
00:04:48,340 --> 00:04:50,360
Weren't you supposed to be
in a meeting at headquarters?

86
00:04:50,780 --> 00:04:53,160
It ended,
and I'm heading back to the police box.

87
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:55,320
Ryotsu,
are you planning to take the day off today?

88
00:04:55,320 --> 00:04:57,000
No, well, I'm listening.

89
00:04:58,540 --> 00:04:59,960
Wait, the whole conversation up until now...

90
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:01,500
You were listening to all of it?

91
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:05,499
Ryotsu!
Get back to the police box immediately!

92
00:05:05,549 --> 00:05:08,820
If you arrive after us, you're fired!

93
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:10,800
That's not fair!

94
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:13,040
There's no such thing, no such thing!

95
00:05:13,420 --> 00:05:15,420
Nakagawa! Where are you driving right now?

96
00:05:16,040 --> 00:05:17,560
I'm near Aoto Station. Right now,

97
00:05:17,610 --> 00:05:20,360
I'm stuck in traffic,
but I'll get out of it soon!

98
00:05:20,640 --> 00:05:24,000
What? Aoto? I see. I'm hanging up!

99
00:05:36,700 --> 00:05:37,380
I can't keep this up.

100
00:05:39,760 --> 00:05:40,160
Thank you very much.

101
00:05:41,540 --> 00:05:43,360
I guess I'll take a taxi from here.

102
00:05:44,100 --> 00:05:44,820
Alright,

103
00:05:44,820 --> 00:05:45,640
let's go!

104
00:05:47,620 --> 00:05:48,160
Floor it!

105
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:51,500
Take me to Kameari Kōen-mae,
the birthplace of Earth!

106
00:05:52,520 --> 00:05:53,700
Excuse me.

107
00:05:54,360 --> 00:05:57,480
I'm not very familiar with this area,
you see.

108
00:05:57,480 --> 00:06:00,120
If you're in a hurry,
please take another taxi.

109
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:03,280
We're fighting every single second here!

110
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:05,840
Move over! I'll drive!

111
00:06:06,040 --> 00:06:06,200
Whoa!

112
00:06:11,600 --> 00:06:12,640
Out of the way, out of the way!

113
00:06:12,840 --> 00:06:13,260
Whoa!

114
00:06:13,620 --> 00:06:15,220
Aaah! Watch out!

115
00:06:15,540 --> 00:06:17,700
Hey, please obey the speed limit!

116
00:06:18,360 --> 00:06:20,040
Shut up! I'm a police officer!

117
00:06:20,300 --> 00:06:23,840
From now on, this car is being
used as an emergency vehicle!

118
00:06:24,620 --> 00:06:25,020
No way!

119
00:06:25,600 --> 00:06:25,900
Whoa!

120
00:06:28,740 --> 00:06:32,020
Damn it! Why does traffic have
to jam up at a time like this!

121
00:06:33,280 --> 00:06:34,000
Take another route.

122
00:06:41,480 --> 00:06:43,860
That road's a no U-turn, isn't it?

123
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:46,620
That was a V-turn, so it's fine.

124
00:06:46,620 --> 00:06:47,740
Really?

125
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:56,240
Pardon the intrusion.

126
00:07:00,700 --> 00:07:03,840
Is it really okay to drive
through someone's garden?

127
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:07,360
People in the old town have warm hearts.
They'll overlook it.

128
00:07:07,360 --> 00:07:09,960
Hey, push the train!

129
00:07:11,340 --> 00:07:13,220
You don't look like it, though.

130
00:07:13,220 --> 00:07:16,400
Shut up! We're going down the stairs,
so hang on tight!

131
00:07:17,080 --> 00:07:17,760
Stairs!

132
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:20,000
Whoa!

133
00:07:20,060 --> 00:07:20,820
Whoa!

134
00:07:21,380 --> 00:07:22,180
Whoa!

135
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:22,760
Whoa!

136
00:07:24,960 --> 00:07:25,760
Whoa!

137
00:07:26,420 --> 00:07:27,300
Dead end!

138
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:28,880
There's an alley!

139
00:07:29,220 --> 00:07:30,720
It's too narrow, we can't get through!

140
00:07:30,880 --> 00:07:33,300
There's no such word as
"impossible" in my dictionary!

141
00:07:34,340 --> 00:07:34,880
Whoa!

142
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:36,660
We're sideways! We're sideways!

143
00:07:36,740 --> 00:07:38,240
Whoa!

144
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:41,120
The wall's breaking! The wall!

145
00:07:41,380 --> 00:07:43,940
People in Kitamachi are warm-hearted,
so it's fine!

146
00:07:43,940 --> 00:07:47,860
Even when a festival mikoshi knocks down a fence,
not a single person around here gets fussy!

147
00:07:48,580 --> 00:07:50,840
This isn't a mikoshi, you know!

148
00:08:01,620 --> 00:08:04,460
Looks like we got here before
Nakagawa and the others.

149
00:08:05,940 --> 00:08:07,080
Sir.

150
00:08:07,080 --> 00:08:08,840
If it's a tip, you can keep it.

151
00:08:08,840 --> 00:08:11,220
Not that. The taxi fare?

152
00:08:11,220 --> 00:08:15,120
I drove here myself,
and I still have to pay?

153
00:08:15,120 --> 00:08:17,240
This doesn't add up.

154
00:08:17,240 --> 00:08:18,320
Here you go.

155
00:08:18,940 --> 00:08:19,420
Thank you very much.

156
00:08:22,100 --> 00:08:24,040
You should have learned the back roads.

157
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:30,200
Chief, hello.

158
00:08:30,200 --> 00:08:33,020
Senpai, you made it in good time.

159
00:08:33,020 --> 00:08:34,300
I'm going to lose my head.

160
00:08:34,300 --> 00:08:35,100
No, no, no.

161
00:08:35,100 --> 00:08:38,940
I'm the type who always
gives my all to my work.

162
00:08:38,940 --> 00:08:42,720
You rushed over from the boatrace venue,
yet you talk so big.

163
00:08:43,480 --> 00:08:45,320
I'm terribly sorry.

164
00:08:45,320 --> 00:08:46,300
Chief.

165
00:08:46,300 --> 00:08:49,820
You have a call from the station chief.

166
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:52,100
What? From the station chief?

167
00:08:53,260 --> 00:08:54,340
What did you say?

168
00:08:54,640 --> 00:08:56,260
R-Ryo... you mean Ryotsu?

169
00:08:58,440 --> 00:08:59,580
Understood.

170
00:08:59,580 --> 00:09:01,340
We'll be there right away.

171
00:09:02,300 --> 00:09:04,680
Chief, has something happened?

172
00:09:05,400 --> 00:09:07,900
One of the suspects in
that taxi robbery case

173
00:09:07,900 --> 00:09:11,520
has reportedly been hiding somewhere in Katsushika Ward.
We've received a tip.

174
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:12,760
Really?

175
00:09:13,280 --> 00:09:15,580
A special task force is being set up,

176
00:09:15,580 --> 00:09:18,460
so all three of you,
come to the station with me.

177
00:09:18,460 --> 00:09:18,960
Yes.

178
00:09:21,880 --> 00:09:24,300
Is this taxi real?

179
00:09:24,880 --> 00:09:25,240
That's right.

180
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:30,240
With the cooperation of a taxi company that
regularly works together with the police,

181
00:09:30,240 --> 00:09:32,140
they've borrowed three cabs.

182
00:09:32,140 --> 00:09:37,260
Using these cars, I want you to
make sure you catch the taxi robber.

183
00:09:37,260 --> 00:09:41,960
But why would you have this idiot
take on such an important mission?

184
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:43,820
Calling me an idiot is a bit much, Chief.

185
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:47,880
Well, it's because of driving skill and
the fact that you hold a Class 2 license.

186
00:09:47,880 --> 00:09:50,740
We had the computer choose the right people,

187
00:09:50,740 --> 00:09:52,377
Nakagawa, Reiko,

188
00:09:52,427 --> 00:09:55,380
and Ryotsu. Those were the three it picked.

189
00:09:56,560 --> 00:10:00,400
So the computer has a far
better eye for people than you do

190
00:10:02,140 --> 00:10:03,040
Sorry to keep you waiting.

191
00:10:05,440 --> 00:10:06,800
We've changed into our uniforms.

192
00:10:07,580 --> 00:10:09,380
You two look great.

193
00:10:09,380 --> 00:10:10,000
Thank you.

194
00:10:13,120 --> 00:10:17,300
If push comes to shove, this
bulletproof glass will protect the driver.

195
00:10:17,920 --> 00:10:18,320
Wow.

196
00:10:18,920 --> 00:10:20,760
I'm counting on you two.

197
00:10:20,760 --> 00:10:21,400
Yes, sir.

198
00:10:21,400 --> 00:10:23,940
Chief, where's my taxi?

199
00:10:24,880 --> 00:10:25,860
This way.

200
00:10:31,800 --> 00:10:34,020
This one is your taxi.

201
00:10:34,020 --> 00:10:37,360
Why is mine the only
old-model clunker like this?

202
00:10:37,800 --> 00:10:41,080
It's not like you have any work to do.
This is the only one we could borrow.

203
00:10:46,100 --> 00:10:49,300
Chief, how about the glass buttons?

204
00:10:49,300 --> 00:10:51,160
Yours doesn't have them.

205
00:10:52,500 --> 00:10:55,400
What if I get targeted with a handgun?

206
00:10:55,980 --> 00:10:58,820
I don't think you'd die even if you got shot,
you know.

207
00:10:58,820 --> 00:11:01,320
Well, just dodge it then.

208
00:11:01,320 --> 00:11:02,540
That's cruel.

209
00:11:02,540 --> 00:11:05,440
That's a huge difference in treatment compared to Nakagawa,
isn't it?

210
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:08,900
I'm off.

211
00:11:13,520 --> 00:11:14,880
I'm off.

212
00:11:24,420 --> 00:11:27,500
Where's Ryotsu?
I thought he'd be here by now.

213
00:11:29,140 --> 00:11:31,000
Move, move, move, move, move!

214
00:11:31,800 --> 00:11:33,100
See you!

215
00:11:35,540 --> 00:11:36,740
We hit something.

216
00:11:36,740 --> 00:11:38,140
And it was a police car, too.

217
00:11:38,580 --> 00:11:40,660
You idiot! Where are you looking?

218
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:44,220
But you can't blame me,
they suddenly jumped out in front of me!

219
00:11:44,620 --> 00:11:45,200
What did you say?

220
00:11:45,880 --> 00:11:47,680
There's an old saying about this, you know!

221
00:11:47,880 --> 00:11:49,920
A car can't stop on a dime, you know!

222
00:11:50,420 --> 00:11:52,060
You move, you're the one who should!

223
00:11:52,100 --> 00:11:52,540
Idiot!

224
00:11:52,800 --> 00:11:54,380
S-sorry...

225
00:11:54,380 --> 00:11:54,880
Right?

226
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:57,580
A-are you really,
really sure it's going to be okay?

227
00:11:57,800 --> 00:12:01,400
Did that computer really pick those guys?

228
00:12:01,540 --> 00:12:03,220
We'd be in trouble if the
million isn't kept separate.

229
00:12:30,560 --> 00:12:32,480
Nakagawa, can you hear me?

230
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:33,320
Yes.

231
00:12:33,920 --> 00:12:37,440
The wanted man is likely inside.

232
00:12:37,440 --> 00:12:38,180
Roger.

233
00:12:38,720 --> 00:12:40,640
He might be moving around by taxi.

234
00:12:41,080 --> 00:12:42,460
If the culprit gets in

235
00:12:42,460 --> 00:12:45,200
act casual and head to wherever you're told.

236
00:13:16,320 --> 00:13:17,620
Let's step on it a little.

237
00:13:37,340 --> 00:13:38,540
We're here.

238
00:13:40,520 --> 00:13:42,500
Arriving in three minutes!

239
00:13:42,500 --> 00:13:43,620
Thank you, you saved me.

240
00:13:44,220 --> 00:13:45,220
How much do I owe you?

241
00:13:45,780 --> 00:13:47,720
I forgot to turn on the meter.

242
00:13:48,180 --> 00:13:49,680
Don't worry, it's free.

243
00:13:49,680 --> 00:13:50,760
No way, I couldn't.

244
00:13:51,260 --> 00:13:54,200
Then keep the change from this.

245
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:54,700
What?

246
00:13:56,120 --> 00:13:58,420
That's a tip for getting here quickly.

247
00:13:58,420 --> 00:14:00,480
Thanks a lot, as always.

248
00:14:01,120 --> 00:14:03,480
5,000 yen for three minutes,
that's a sweet deal.

249
00:14:05,160 --> 00:14:06,720
Take me to Haneda.

250
00:14:07,640 --> 00:14:09,040
That's a bit too far.

251
00:14:09,040 --> 00:14:10,100
No, no way.

252
00:14:10,520 --> 00:14:12,740
Please, my flight's time is coming up.

253
00:14:14,160 --> 00:14:15,900
Make it 10,000 yen.

254
00:14:15,900 --> 00:14:17,160
10,000 yen?

255
00:14:17,160 --> 00:14:19,100
Alright, deal.

256
00:14:19,100 --> 00:14:21,780
Taking the expressway from Kosugi is faster.

257
00:14:21,780 --> 00:14:23,300
Hold on tight.

258
00:14:32,300 --> 00:14:33,100
What's wrong?

259
00:14:33,100 --> 00:14:35,520
The wanted man has come out.

260
00:14:35,920 --> 00:14:36,320
What?

261
00:14:36,320 --> 00:14:38,000
He's trying to go somewhere.

262
00:14:38,840 --> 00:14:39,640
Right then.

263
00:14:39,640 --> 00:14:41,160
Wait for him where he comes out, and...

264
00:14:44,960 --> 00:14:46,940
Ryotsu's cab isn't here.

265
00:14:46,940 --> 00:14:47,340
What?

266
00:14:47,340 --> 00:14:49,020
Where's Ryotsu?

267
00:14:49,020 --> 00:14:51,820
Looks like he picked up a
passenger and left somewhere.

268
00:14:51,820 --> 00:14:53,400
What is he doing?

269
00:14:53,400 --> 00:14:54,720
That idiot!

270
00:14:54,720 --> 00:14:56,720
Damn it.

271
00:14:56,720 --> 00:14:58,900
He got into a different taxi.

272
00:15:00,800 --> 00:15:02,180
The plan's a bust.

273
00:15:02,180 --> 00:15:04,020
Ryotsu, respond!

274
00:15:04,020 --> 00:15:04,820
Ryotsu!

275
00:15:05,420 --> 00:15:08,140
Damn it, he's turned off his radio.

276
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:15,180
Driving by instinct is faster than looking at a navigation system,
you know.

277
00:15:15,180 --> 00:15:16,500
Impressive, as expected.

278
00:15:16,940 --> 00:15:18,920
Have you been doing this job long?

279
00:15:19,740 --> 00:15:20,880
Since today.

280
00:15:22,880 --> 00:15:24,180
We've got a customer.

281
00:15:24,180 --> 00:15:27,600
Alright, time to go do some business.

282
00:15:27,600 --> 00:15:28,720
See you.

283
00:15:29,780 --> 00:15:30,640
Alright then.

284
00:15:31,200 --> 00:15:33,140
For luggage, a truck is better.

285
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:34,440
Excuse me.

286
00:15:35,540 --> 00:15:36,740
Heading out from Shibamata.

287
00:15:38,140 --> 00:15:40,120
I'm going to the museum, you see.

288
00:15:40,120 --> 00:15:42,860
Are you two visiting
Tokyo for the first time?

289
00:15:42,860 --> 00:15:45,060
Yes, so where should we start?

290
00:15:45,060 --> 00:15:46,600
If we start from Odaiba,

291
00:15:46,600 --> 00:15:48,060
it's close from here.

292
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:50,940
Excuse me a moment.

293
00:15:52,100 --> 00:15:52,500
Yes.

294
00:15:53,160 --> 00:15:55,040
Senpai, where are you?

295
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:56,600
The Chief is absolutely furious!

296
00:15:57,700 --> 00:15:59,120
It's Nakagawa.

297
00:15:59,720 --> 00:16:02,080
Sorry, but I've got a customer right now.

298
00:16:02,080 --> 00:16:04,420
You two take care of that side.

299
00:16:04,420 --> 00:16:05,820
But that's...

300
00:16:06,560 --> 00:16:09,080
Is Harajuku close?

301
00:16:09,400 --> 00:16:10,960
It's close, it's close!

302
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:12,580
Then let's head that way.

303
00:16:12,580 --> 00:16:14,640
I can't use a phone while driving.

304
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:15,380
I'm hanging up.

305
00:16:15,380 --> 00:16:17,680
Well then, let's go.

306
00:16:17,680 --> 00:16:19,200
Please take good care of us.

307
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:24,220
Honestly, that Ryotsu.

308
00:16:24,220 --> 00:16:26,280
Where on earth did he run off to?

309
00:16:26,280 --> 00:16:28,820
That's a borrowed taxi, isn't it?

310
00:16:28,820 --> 00:16:33,220
Assigning someone like Ryotsu to such an
important mission was a mistake from the start.

311
00:16:33,220 --> 00:16:35,160
Yes, sir, you're absolutely right.

312
00:16:35,820 --> 00:16:38,300
Move aside, move aside!
Ryotsu Taxi coming through!

313
00:16:39,740 --> 00:16:42,020
Is it all right to force your
way into the traffic jam like this?

314
00:16:42,300 --> 00:16:45,260
Sure, sure! All the roads belong to me!

315
00:16:47,460 --> 00:16:50,300
Hey! You in the police car ahead!
Get out of the way, you bastard!

316
00:16:51,020 --> 00:16:55,320
What kind of driver flashes
his headlights at a police car?

317
00:16:57,200 --> 00:16:58,000
Ryotsu!

318
00:16:58,320 --> 00:16:59,120
See? Heartless!

319
00:16:59,420 --> 00:17:00,560
Uh-oh, this is bad!

320
00:17:06,640 --> 00:17:08,140
Unbelievable guy.

321
00:17:09,260 --> 00:17:10,360
Thank you very much.

322
00:17:11,420 --> 00:17:13,720
Watch out for creepy pickup artists, okay?

323
00:17:14,280 --> 00:17:14,640
Yes.

324
00:17:15,060 --> 00:17:15,760
See ya.

325
00:17:18,500 --> 00:17:21,140
Making 20,000 yen in under two hours,

326
00:17:21,140 --> 00:17:23,060
this is a great business.

327
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:25,340
Alright, I've decided.

328
00:17:27,520 --> 00:17:29,780
Is this really okay? Modifying it this much?

329
00:17:30,520 --> 00:17:33,600
This car's borrowed from
the taxi company, right?

330
00:17:33,600 --> 00:17:36,420
I've got my severance pay coming,
so I figured I'd take it.

331
00:17:36,420 --> 00:17:37,380
Don't mind, it's fine.

332
00:17:37,900 --> 00:17:39,020
Retirement pay, though?

333
00:17:39,020 --> 00:17:39,680
Ryo-san,

334
00:17:39,680 --> 00:17:41,080
you're quitting the police force?

335
00:17:41,080 --> 00:17:42,120
You bet I am.

336
00:17:42,120 --> 00:17:43,260
This pays

337
00:17:43,260 --> 00:17:44,700
a whole lot more money, you know.

338
00:17:44,700 --> 00:17:47,300
Ryo-san knows the back roads well,
after all.

339
00:17:47,300 --> 00:17:47,860
Yeah.

340
00:17:47,860 --> 00:17:49,400
Maybe it's a career change.

341
00:17:50,660 --> 00:17:52,060
Yeah, maybe it is.

342
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:53,720
Well then.

343
00:17:54,640 --> 00:17:55,900
Modification costs, pfft,

344
00:17:55,900 --> 00:17:58,120
I'll earn that back in two or three days,
just watch.

345
00:17:58,120 --> 00:18:01,920
Those guys

346
00:18:01,920 --> 00:18:03,020
somewhere...

347
00:18:11,440 --> 00:18:13,760
Sure enough, he's the taxi robber.

348
00:18:14,820 --> 00:18:17,620
He walked right into the cage on his own!

349
00:18:17,620 --> 00:18:20,220
Hey, take me to Narita Airport.

350
00:18:20,220 --> 00:18:21,600
That customer...

351
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:25,740
Actually, vicious taxi robberies
have been going around lately.

352
00:18:25,740 --> 00:18:27,460
I'm sorry, but

353
00:18:27,460 --> 00:18:30,180
Could you pay the fare up front?

354
00:18:30,180 --> 00:18:30,720
What?

355
00:18:31,840 --> 00:18:32,640
Stop it.

356
00:18:34,220 --> 00:18:36,300
Fine, I suppose it can't be helped.

357
00:18:36,300 --> 00:18:37,340
How much?

358
00:18:37,340 --> 00:18:39,240
I'll knock it down to 20,000 yen.

359
00:18:41,260 --> 00:18:41,840
Thanks as always.

360
00:18:48,440 --> 00:18:49,720
He's got a gun

361
00:18:49,720 --> 00:18:50,720
The one on the right.

362
00:19:01,140 --> 00:19:02,020
What's wrong?

363
00:19:04,120 --> 00:19:05,780
The crime-prevention light is on.

364
00:19:05,780 --> 00:19:07,760
Something might have happened.

365
00:19:08,200 --> 00:19:08,980
Let's pull him over.

366
00:19:11,340 --> 00:19:12,620
That's a stop signal.

367
00:19:16,400 --> 00:19:17,720
Your license, please.

368
00:19:18,440 --> 00:19:19,160
Yeah, yeah.

369
00:19:30,060 --> 00:19:31,560
Sorry, sir.

370
00:19:50,080 --> 00:19:50,840
Run!

371
00:19:52,520 --> 00:19:53,000
Run!

372
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:53,260
Run!

373
00:19:53,260 --> 00:19:53,480
Run!

374
00:19:54,060 --> 00:19:54,580
Run!

375
00:19:54,580 --> 00:19:54,600
Run!

376
00:19:54,600 --> 00:19:55,520
Run!

377
00:19:58,640 --> 00:19:59,200
Run!

378
00:19:59,200 --> 00:19:59,520
Run!

379
00:19:59,520 --> 00:19:59,540
Run!

380
00:19:59,540 --> 00:19:59,580
Run!

381
00:20:01,440 --> 00:20:03,540
Run!

382
00:20:06,560 --> 00:20:08,040
Get out of the way!

383
00:20:12,780 --> 00:20:15,280
Senpai, you really did well.

384
00:20:15,280 --> 00:20:18,540
No matter what they say,
you really come through when it counts.

385
00:20:18,540 --> 00:20:19,340
Ryo-chan.

386
00:20:19,340 --> 00:20:22,240
I'm glad I got to do one
last good deed for the force.

387
00:20:24,240 --> 00:20:27,360
Chief, thank you for all
your help over the years.

388
00:20:28,660 --> 00:20:29,940
What? A resignation letter?

389
00:20:29,940 --> 00:20:32,720
Hey, what's going on here?

390
00:20:33,560 --> 00:20:37,480
I've realized that driving
a taxi is my true calling.

391
00:20:40,360 --> 00:20:41,220
Well then,

392
00:20:42,980 --> 00:20:44,820
Hey, Ryo-zu!

393
00:20:46,400 --> 00:20:50,300
Hey, wait! That taxi is borrowed, you know!

394
00:20:50,300 --> 00:20:51,860
You idiot!

395
00:20:51,860 --> 00:20:54,280
This is bad!

396
00:20:54,740 --> 00:20:56,120
What's going on?

397
00:20:56,120 --> 00:20:58,000
Take a look at this.

398
00:20:58,000 --> 00:20:59,240
What is it?

399
00:21:00,960 --> 00:21:02,500
Damage reports.

400
00:21:03,560 --> 00:21:05,380
These are from the damage
Ryotsu's taxi caused.

401
00:21:05,380 --> 00:21:09,140
And there are countless more
reports of traffic violations.

402
00:21:09,140 --> 00:21:11,140
Damn you, Ryotsu!

403
00:21:11,940 --> 00:21:15,840
Nakagawa, Reiko, go nab Ryotsu right away!

404
00:21:15,840 --> 00:21:16,440
Yes, sir!

405
00:21:21,120 --> 00:21:24,280
I'm not going to put up with being
a civil servant on a measly salary!

406
00:21:24,760 --> 00:21:28,620
From now on, I'm going to rake
in the money with this taxi alone!

407
00:21:30,280 --> 00:21:30,660
Gah!

408
00:21:36,880 --> 00:21:37,700
Crap!

409
00:21:37,700 --> 00:21:40,080
Taxi ahead, stop right now!

410
00:21:40,620 --> 00:21:41,700
No way!

411
00:21:41,700 --> 00:21:43,280
I'm going to lose them!

412
00:21:52,840 --> 00:21:53,760
Damn it!

413
00:21:53,760 --> 00:21:55,620
Those guys are so persistent!

414
00:22:03,560 --> 00:22:04,746
Heh heh, how about that?

415
00:22:04,796 --> 00:22:07,580
Bet you spent a fortune
modifying it Damn it.

416
00:22:08,760 --> 00:22:09,740
W-what?!

417
00:22:12,460 --> 00:22:14,240
I won't let you get away, senpai!

418
00:22:14,440 --> 00:22:15,560
N-Nakagawa!

419
00:22:15,800 --> 00:22:17,640
Ryo-chan, stop the car!

420
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:20,260
Ryo-chan, give up already!

421
00:22:20,460 --> 00:22:22,728
As expected of a top driver,

422
00:22:22,778 --> 00:22:24,740
dodging the oil attack like that!

423
00:22:24,740 --> 00:22:26,540
Come on, please stop!

424
00:22:27,040 --> 00:22:29,360
No way, Kintaro!

425
00:22:43,280 --> 00:22:46,740
You'll never catch these wheels!

426
00:22:46,740 --> 00:22:47,920
Akechi-kun

427
00:22:50,240 --> 00:22:52,760
It's like James Bond's car in 007!

428
00:22:52,760 --> 00:22:52,980
Damn it!

429
00:22:52,980 --> 00:22:54,380
Oh my.

430
00:22:54,380 --> 00:22:56,760
But up ahead, isn't it...

431
00:22:58,100 --> 00:23:00,260
Looks like they've given up.

432
00:23:00,260 --> 00:23:02,060
There's no road!

433
00:23:03,560 --> 00:23:04,800
Aaaaaah!

434
00:23:04,800 --> 00:23:05,260
Aaaaaah!

435
00:23:17,200 --> 00:23:20,020
Senpai, what on earth happened?

436
00:23:22,080 --> 00:23:25,120
The car just went, like, boom and...

437
00:23:25,120 --> 00:23:29,640
I was thinking about getting back to regular duty soon,
or something.

438
00:23:29,640 --> 00:23:31,840
Your resignation letter
has already been accepted.

439
00:23:33,560 --> 00:23:35,320
Good work, Ryotsu.

440
00:23:35,320 --> 00:23:37,160
Um, Chief?

441
00:23:37,160 --> 00:23:42,580
The bills have arrived from the people
whose hedges were destroyed by the taxi,

442
00:23:42,580 --> 00:23:44,300
so make sure you pay them.

443
00:23:46,520 --> 00:23:49,660
And that taxi was borrowed, you know.

444
00:23:49,660 --> 00:23:52,280
Be sure to return it to the taxi company.

445
00:23:52,720 --> 00:23:53,120
No way...

446
00:23:56,320 --> 00:23:57,120
Hidden...

447
00:24:24,300 --> 00:24:25,820
Quite right.

448
00:24:27,020 --> 00:24:30,520
But I act all cool with one hand,

449
00:24:30,520 --> 00:24:33,280
beef bowl, extra sauce, extra soaked.

450
00:24:33,280 --> 00:24:36,640
Overtime-streak frustration too,

451
00:24:36,640 --> 00:24:40,220
frustration gone in a flash.

452
00:24:43,540 --> 00:24:46,320
Every day is no problem.

453
00:24:46,320 --> 00:24:50,000
Once I've gone through a hot shower,

454
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:53,040
every day is no problem.

455
00:24:54,300 --> 00:24:56,560
A pillow restores my energy.

456
00:24:59,820 --> 00:25:02,480
Every day is no program.

457
00:25:02,480 --> 00:25:06,200
I love myself just the way I am.

458
00:25:06,200 --> 00:25:09,440
Every day, no plans at all.

459
00:25:09,440 --> 00:25:13,000
Monday, with hearts floating all around.

460
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:17,240
Every day, no plans at all.

461
00:25:17,240 --> 00:25:22,940
Listen up, Kameari King-O!

462
00:25:24,300 --> 00:25:25,860
Repay my kindness for
all the money I raised.

463
00:25:25,860 --> 00:25:29,900
Become a fine racehorse
and rake in the winnings!

464
00:25:29,900 --> 00:25:33,280
You're going to become a
star of Nakayama Racecourse.

465
00:25:33,280 --> 00:25:36,100
Run next time, Kameari King-O!

466
00:25:36,100 --> 00:25:37,180
Count on you.

467
00:25:38,520 --> 00:25:40,460
Over there is Kameari.

468
00:25:41,760 --> 00:25:43,820
Well, it's definitely Kameari.

469
00:25:45,380 --> 00:25:49,140
Everyone, come on over to our town!

470
00:25:50,260 --> 00:25:50,700
Thank you.

